  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reform of the Water Infrastructure sector in Mauritius</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mauritius has well developed water supply infrastructure. Deferred investments, poor maintenance coupled with limited capacity in infrastructure planning, implementation and management, however, has resulted in its deterioration over time. Despite high annual rainfall, challenges persist within the water sector. These include intermittent water supply, high non-revenue water losses, water pollution, reduced food security and overlapped institutional arrangements. Growing water demands and climate change combine to compound these challenges. It is therefore imperative for Mauritius to invest in the review, analysis and improvement of its water infrastructure leading to a well-planned, managed and sustainably operated system.

Implementing partner: Climate Resilient Infrastructure Development Facility (CRIDF)</narrative>
  </description>
